Actionable error-handling finding at input.rs:5 (ERR-01): unwrap() turns expected missing/unreadable user configuration into a panic. Propagate the I/O error instead:

```rust
use std::fs;
use std::io;
use std::path::Path;

pub fn load_config(path: &Path) -> io::Result<String> {
    fs::read_to_string(path)
}
```

Callers can propagate with ? or display an error that includes the path. Result preserves the failure cause; Option would discard useful diagnostics, and replacing unwrap with expect would still panic on a recoverable failure. Review/proposal only; no filesystem behavior tests run.

Replace the indexed lookup at input.py:4 with dict.get:

```python
LANGUAGES = {"rust": ".rs", "python": ".py"}

def extension(language):
    return LANGUAGES.get(language)
```

Known keys retain their extension values; an unknown key returns None. The Rust skill does not apply to this Python lookup. This is the proposed fix; the evaluation's read-only instruction means the fixture was not edited, and no tests were run.
